# ---- HOST-NATIVE STATION (native from day one — cpm22 wave, 2026-09-20) ----
# MAME 0.289's kayproii driver runs ON THE HOST — drawshm frames, ctlsock
# keys through the generated keymap, no audio, no network. Launcher: shared
# stations/mame-native/x11-runtime.sh; reset = relaunch restoring the golden
# savestate (kayproii has MACHINE_SUPPORTS_SAVE).
#
# CORRECTION vs the integration seed: the driver is `kayproii`, not
# `kaypro2` (that string is only formats/kaypro_dsk.cpp's floppy-format
# name) — confirmed with -listxml on a stock MAME 0.276 system package,
# 2026-09-20.
SH_RESET_MODE=relaunch
SH_FIXTURE_DESC=Kaypro II CP/M 2.2 (GMv2.72) boot floppy -- the A> prompt with the disk's own STANDARD/PRINTER software directory already visible (ASM/BAUD/DDT/DUMP/ED/LOAD/MOVCPM/PIP/STAT/SUBMIT/SYSGEN/...), drawn on the native 560x240 MAME raster by MAME 0.289's kayproii running HOST-NATIVE (drawshm). MEASURED 2026-09-20 on a stock MAME 0.276 system package (bios 149c, NOT yet re-measured on the fleet-pinned 0.289 native binary): cold boot reaches the A> prompt in ~6 emulated seconds with no automation needed (the CP/M boot floppy prints its own directory at boot), and a scripted `DIR\n` through MAME's natural-keyboard path re-ran the listing cleanly. Keyboard is HLE'd via an Intel 8049 MCU (device kaypro10kbd, its own separate ROM set) rather than a CPU-scanned matrix the driver polls directly -- unlike samcoupe/zxspectrum/mpf2/bbcmicro/dragon32, so it is OPEN whether MAME_CTL_KEY_EXCL is needed here; measure on the fleet binary before shipping the type-in demo. No pointer: the Kaypro II has no mouse port. No audio: MAME_NATIVE_ARGS carries none and SH_AUDIO is off.
MAME_NATIVE_BIN=/data/vms/streamhost/assets/cpm22/mame-native/kayproii
MAME_NATIVE_DRIVER=kayproii
MAME_NATIVE_ROMS=/data/vms/streamhost/assets/cpm22/mame-native/roms
MAME_NATIVE_GEOM=1024x768
MAME_NATIVE_SKIP_WARNINGS=0
# Golden stream (2026-09-20): NOT yet captured on the fleet-pinned 0.289
# native binary -- see docs/lab/CPM22-WAVE.md for status. Decision: keep =1
# once the golden restore is proven, matching the fleet's other
# MACHINE_SUPPORTS_SAVE MAME-native stations.
MAME_NATIVE_CHECKPOINT=0
# Device set CONFIRMED on a stock MAME 0.276 system package (2026-09-20):
# bios 149c (the default bios "149"/81-149.u47 has no surviving dump on any
# mirror checked), flop1 the CP/M boot disk, flop2 WordStar 3.3. Both media
# files are TOSEC preservation images (.td0/.imd) fed to MAME UNCONVERTED --
# see scripts/build-guests/tiles/cpm22.sh for why a raw .kay conversion of
# the same boot disk fails (logical sector order).
MAME_NATIVE_ARGS=-bios 149c -flop1 /data/vms/streamhost/assets/cpm22/media/cpm22-boot.td0 -flop2 /data/vms/streamhost/assets/cpm22/media/wordstar33.imd
SH_MAMECTL_SOCK=/data/vms/streamhost/stations/cpm22/ctl.sock
SH_MAMESOCK_KEYMAP=/data/vms/streamhost/stations/cpm22/cpm22.keymap

# ---- STANDBY (instant-ready: an emulator nobody watches costs ~0 CPU) ----
SH_IDLE_PAUSE_SECS=60
SH_IDLE_PAUSE_PIDFILE=/data/vms/streamhost/stations/cpm22/mame.pid
SH_IDLE_PAUSE_PROC_MATCH=assets/cpm22/mame-native
MAME_NATIVE_STANDBY_DELAY_S=8

# ---- KEYBOARD (Intel 8049 MCU HLE, device kaypro10kbd) ----
# Fleet floor 40/40 ms first (bumped to samcoupe's measured 80/80 below,
# since this driver's own keyboard device is an MCU HLE this wave has not
# yet stress-tested the same way samcoupe's CPU-scanned matrix was).
# MAME_CTL_KEY_EXCL is OPEN -- see SH_FIXTURE_DESC above.
SH_KEY_MIN_HOLD_MS=80
SH_KEY_MIN_GAP_MS=80

# ---- POINTER: none. The Kaypro II has no mouse port on this machine. ----
